const schema = [{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Service","name":"Physician Writing Services","serviceType":"Research, analysis, publication and communication support for practising clinicians","provider":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Pubrica","url":"https://pubrica.com/"},"url":"https://pubrica.com/services/physician-writing-services/","description":"Nine research, publication and communication services for clinicians, each with its price and scope cap published.","areaServed":"Worldwide","audience":{"@type":"Audience","audienceType":"Researchers, PhD scholars, research institutions, medical writers and life-science teams"}},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do physicians publish research alongside a full clinical load?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"By deciding what to hand over and what only they can do, and the split is more lopsided than most people expect. A full clinical manuscript takes a practising doctor somewhere between forty and eighty hours, spread across months of interrupted evenings, and published estimates in the medical writing field put it at forty to fifty hours even for a professional. The parts only you can do — the question, the clinical judgement, the interpretation, the decision about what the data may claim — are a small fraction of that. The rest is assembly, referencing, formatting, checklist completion and journal correspondence. Two practical things also help regardless of who writes it: decide the article type from the data before drafting rather than from what the last paper was, and write the author list down in week one against the four ICMJE criteria. Both take an hour and both prevent the expensive problems."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which of your nine services do I need?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The router at the top of this page answers it in four questions, and the answer follows from what you physically have rather than from what you want to end up with. One patient is a case report. Ten or more from a defined population is a study with a denominator, and writing it as a series throws the denominator away. A dataset needs the article type settling before anything else. A study not yet run needs a protocol and an ethics set. A question for the literature needs the review type chosen, because the gap between a scoping review and a systematic review is a factor of three in cost and a different conclusion. A draft usually needs structure rather than language. And everything else — the board paper, the talk, the rebuttal — is customized writing. If the router puts you on a page and the page looks wrong, ask us; we would rather move you than take the brief."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to declare that somebody helped write it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, and the declaration is what makes the arrangement legitimate rather than what exposes it. The ICMJE lists writing assistance, technical editing, language editing and proofreading among the activities that on their own do not qualify somebody for authorship, says such contributors should be acknowledged with their specific contribution described, and advises editors to require the corresponding author to obtain written permission from everybody acknowledged. It also requires disclosure of a sponsor’s role in the writing of the report. So a Pubrica writer is named in the acknowledgements, we supply both the wording and the permission, and you keep authorship. Where a contribution genuinely meets all four criteria we say so and let you decide — nothing bars a writer from being an author; it is the contribution that decides, not the invoice. Ghostwriting is undisclosed authorship. Declared assistance is the opposite of it, not a polite version."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you guarantee my paper will be published?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, and neither can anybody else. Acceptance is an editor’s decision informed by reviewers, and a supplier promising it is selling you something they do not control. We also do not offer “unlimited revisions until acceptance”, which is the same promise in a different coat: it ties a fixed fee to an outcome outside the contract and is unenforceable in the direction that matters to you. What we commit to instead is what we can actually deliver — 365 days of uncapped revision inside the agreed scope on the manuscript services, from the date of delivery, so that a reviewer asking for a reanalysis eight months later is covered. We will also tell you at the quote stage when we think a study cannot support the paper you want, which occasionally ends an engagement before it starts. That is a better outcome than a well-written manuscript for a study that will be returned."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you price, and why publish it at all?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every price in this section is a floor with its scope cap printed beside it — a word count, a reference count, a database count, a piece count. We publish them because this market almost entirely does not: when we checked on 21 September 2026, editing was densely and openly priced everywhere and writing was behind a contact form nearly universally. For case report writing, literature searching and patient education content we could not find a single provider anywhere publishing a price. Where a comparator does exist we name it on the page and sit below it; where none exists we say that too, rather than implying a comparison that is not there. The honest reason to publish is that a clinician should be able to find out whether something is affordable without a sales conversation, and the honest reason most do not is that a price with a cap beside it is harder to move afterwards."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to my unpublished data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves, and writers and project staff are bound by internal confidentiality agreements as well. Unpublished data, protocols and draft manuscripts are held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, kept only as long as the project needs them, never used to train anything and never shared outside your project team. We do not take competing applications to the same funding call. Where material contains patient identifiers we ask you to remove them before sending rather than removing them ourselves, because what counts as identifiable in your case is a judgement your ethics approval governs — and one specific warning worth repeating: DICOM image headers carry patient names and dates of birth straight through an export, invisible on screen and fully readable to anyone who downloads the file."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you use AI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Declared to you first, and handled to the ICMJE’s guidance as updated in January 2026, which added a section specifically about it. A chatbot cannot be an author, because it cannot be accountable and accountability is one of the four criteria. AI used for writing assistance is disclosed in the acknowledgements. AI used for data collection, analysis or figure generation is described in the methods in enough detail to replicate the approach — the tool, the version and the prompts. AI-generated material is not cited as a primary source. And the failure mode that matters is output that sounds authoritative and is wrong, which is our job to catch rather than yours: everything is checked against sources somebody can open. We also tell you the result of the AI-content screening we run rather than only acting on it, because those tools produce false positives and you should know what a journal might see."}}]},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://pubrica.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Physician writing","item":"https://pubrica.com/services/physician-writing-services/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Physician writing","item":"https://pubrica.com/services/physician-writing-services/"}]}];

